#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum (CLA s 3(1))` (`the September CPI figures I gave` 141 75) EQUALS 4136000
#ASSERT `the prescribed minimum (CLA s 3(1))` (`the September CPI figures I gave` 141.3 75) EQUALS 5180
#ASSERT `the prescribed maximum (CLA s 3(1))` (`the September CPI figures I gave` 141.3 75) EQUALS 4144800

-- The s 52(3)(c) bands at 1.30: 2 000 -> 2 600, 1 000 -> 1 300, 23 000 -> 29 900, 3 000 -> 3 900, 65 000 -> 84 500,
-- 5 000 -> 6 500, 170 000 -> 221 000, 10 000 -> 13 000, 300 000 -> 390 000.
-- ISV 11: 2 600 + 1 x 1 300 = 3 900. ISV 31: 2 600 + 21 x 1 300 = 29 900. ISV 32: 29 900 + 3 900 = 33 800.
-- ISV 45: 29 900 + 14 x 3 900 = 84 500. ISV 50: 84 500 + 5 x 6 500 = 117 000. ISV 66: 84 500 + 21 x 6 500 = 221 000.
-- ISV 70: 221 000 + 4 x 13 000 = 273 000. ISV 78: 221 000 + 12 x 13 000 = 377 000. ISV 79 and 100: 390 000.
#ASSERT `the s 52(3)(c) amount for an injury scale value of` 11 `at` 1.3 EQUALS 3900
#ASSERT `the s 52(3)(c) amount for an injury scale value of` 31 `at` 1.3 EQUALS 29900
#ASSERT `the s 52(3)(c) amount for an injury scale value of` 32 `at` 1.3 EQUALS 33800
#ASSERT `the s 52(3)(c) amount for an injury scale value of` 45 `at` 1.3 EQUALS 84500
#ASSERT `the s 52(3)(c) amount for an injury scale value of` 50 `at` 1.3 EQUALS 117000
#ASSERT `the s 52(3)(c) amount for an injury scale value of` 66 `at` 1.3 EQUALS 221000
#ASSERT `the s 52(3)(c) amount for an injury scale value of` 70 `at` 1.3 EQUALS 273000
#ASSERT `the s 52(3)(c) amount for an injury scale value of` 78 `at` 1.3 EQUALS 377000
#ASSERT `the s 52(3)(c) amount for an injury scale value of` 79 `at` 1.3 EQUALS 390000
#ASSERT `the s 52(3)(c) amount for an injury scale value of` 100 `at` 1.3 EQUALS 390000
-- Each amount rounded separately to $10: at 1.2345, 2 000 -> 2 469, so 2 470; 1 000 -> 1 234.5, so 1 230. ISV 15:
-- 2 470 + 5 x 1 230 = 8 620.
#ASSERT `the s 52(3)(c) amount for an injury scale value of` 15 `at` 1.2345 EQUALS 8620
-- The s 52(7) proportion: an injury on 1 March 2026 takes the 1 July 2025 adjustment (130 / 100); one on 1 March 2014
-- takes the stated amounts (no adjustment before 1 July 2014).
#ASSERT `the s 52(7) proportion for an injury on` `1 Mar 2026` (`the March CPI figures I gave` 130 100) EQUALS 1.3
#ASSERT `the s 52(7) proportion for an injury on` `1 Mar 2014` (`the March CPI figures I gave` 130 100) EQUALS 1

-- The question. Arguments: day; days impaired; medical expenses; ISV; exceptional; ISV used instead; CPI Sept (year
-- before); CPI Sept 2001; CPI March (last 1 July); CPI March 2013.
-- CASE "Dana": ISV 20, 30 days impaired: 2 600 + 10 x 1 300 = 15 600.
#ASSERT `What damages for non-economic loss can I get` `1 Mar 2026` 30 500 20 FALSE 0 141 75 130 100 EQUALS `damages for non-economic loss of` 15600
-- An accident on 1 December 2013 (stated amounts): ISV 20 gives 2 000 + 10 x 1 000 = 12 000; ISV 40 gives 23 000 +
-- 9 x 3 000 = 50 000.
#ASSERT `What damages for non-economic loss can I get` `1 Dec 2013` 30 500 20 FALSE 0 141 75 130 100 EQUALS `damages for non-economic loss of` 12000
#ASSERT `What damages for non-economic loss can I get` `1 Dec 2013` 30 500 40 FALSE 0 141 75 130 100 EQUALS `damages for non-economic loss of` 50000
-- s 52(1): 5 days impaired and $1 000 of medical expenses (under the $5 170 minimum): nothing. 7 days: the threshold is
-- met. $5 170 of medical expenses with 2 days: met too.
#ASSERT `What damages for non-economic loss can I get` `1 Mar 2026` 5 1000 20 FALSE 0 141 75 130 100 EQUALS `none: the s 52(1) threshold is not met`
#ASSERT `What damages for non-economic loss can I get` `1 Mar 2026` 7 1000 20 FALSE 0 141 75 130 100 EQUALS `damages for non-economic loss of` 15600
#ASSERT `What damages for non-economic loss can I get` `1 Mar 2026` 2 5170 20 FALSE 0 141 75 130 100 EQUALS `damages for non-economic loss of` 15600
-- s 52(4): ISV 10 is not over 10. Dana, if her ISV were 10, gets nothing for pain and suffering under either scheme
-- (finding 12).
#ASSERT `What damages for non-economic loss can I get` `1 Mar 2026` 30 500 10 FALSE 0 141 75 130 100 EQUALS `none: the injury scale value is 10 or less (s 52(4))`
-- s 52(5), (6): ISV 9, exceptional; the court uses 11 (22% higher): 3 900. Had it used 10, the bands give nothing.
#ASSERT `What damages for non-economic loss can I get` `1 Mar 2026` 30 500 9 TRUE 11 141 75 130 100 EQUALS `damages for non-economic loss of` 3900
#ASSERT `What damages for non-economic loss can I get` `1 Mar 2026` 30 500 9 TRUE 10 141 75 130 100 EQUALS `none: the s 52(3)(c) bands give no amount for the injury scale value of 10 or less used under s 52(5), (6)`
-- Reg 7 (finding 23, a correction): "An ISV assessed by a court must be expressed as a whole number (a number having a
-- fraction of half or more being rounded up to the nearest whole number)". An assessment of 10.5 is expressed as 11, so
-- 2 600 + 1 x 1 300 = 3 900 (it was asserted `not covered` before). 10.4 is expressed as 10: nothing (s 52(4)). 101 is
-- off the s 52(3)(a) scale.
#ASSERT `What damages for non-economic loss can I get` `1 Mar 2026` 30 500 10.5 FALSE 0 141 75 130 100 EQUALS `damages for non-economic loss of` 3900
#ASSERT `What damages for non-economic loss can I get` `1 Mar 2026` 30 500 10.4 FALSE 0 141 75 130 100 EQUALS `none: the injury scale value is 10 or less (s 52(4))`
#ASSERT `What damages for non-economic loss can I get` `1 Mar 2026` 30 500 101 FALSE 0 141 75 130 100 EQUALS `not covered: an injury scale value must be from 0 to 100 (s 52(3)(a), reg 7)`
-- 30 June 2013 is before the 2013 scheme (LSS Act Sch 2 cl 21(2)); 1 July 2013 is its first day, at the stated amounts
-- (no s 52(7) adjustment before 1 July 2014): ISV 20 gives 2 000 + 10 x 1 000 = 12 000.
#ASSERT `What damages for non-economic loss can I get` `30 Jun 2013` 30 500 20 FALSE 0 141 75 130 100 EQUALS `not covered: an accident before 1 July 2013`
#ASSERT `What damages for non-economic loss can I get` `1 Jul 2013` 30 500 20 FALSE 0 141 75 130 100 EQUALS `damages for non-economic loss of` 12000

-- Mental harm (s 53). Arguments: day of the accident; physically injured; at the scene; close family; recognised
-- psychiatric illness.
#ASSERT `Can I get damages for mental harm` `1 Mar 2026` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `damages may be awarded for the mental harm, but not for economic loss from it (s 53(3))`
#ASSERT `Can I get damages for mental harm` `1 Mar 2026` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `damages may be awarded for the mental harm, and for economic loss from it`
#ASSERT `Can I get damages for mental harm` `1 Mar 2026` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `damages may be awarded for the mental harm, and for economic loss from it`
#ASSERT `Can I get damages for mental harm` `1 Mar 2026` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no damages for the mental harm (s 53(1), (2))`
-- A mother told by phone that her son was killed: not at the scene, but a parent of a person killed (s 53(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `Can I get damages for mental harm` `1 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `damages may be awarded for the mental harm, and for economic loss from it`
#ASSERT `Can I get damages for mental harm` `1 Mar 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no damages for the mental harm (s 53(1), (2))`
-- An accident on 1 December 2012: before the 2013 scheme, so outside this encoding (finding 22: by scope, for s 53).
#ASSERT `Can I get damages for mental harm` `1 Dec 2012` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered: an accident before 1 July 2013`

-- Loss of earning capacity (ss 54, 56A), prescribed maximum 4 136 000. Arguments: day of the accident; past; first week;
-- future; ISV; exceptional; CPI Sept; CPI Sept 2001.
-- Past 52 000 less the first week's 1 000 = 51 000; future 300 000 (ISV 12, over 7): 351 000 x 0.8 = 280 800.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can get for loss of earning capacity` `1 Mar 2026` 52000 1000 300000 12 FALSE 141 75 EQUALS `the most that can be awarded is` 280800
-- ISV 7: no future loss (s 56A(2)): 51 000 x 0.8 = 40 800. Exceptional (s 56A(3)): 280 800.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can get for loss of earning capacity` `1 Mar 2026` 52000 1000 300000 7 FALSE 141 75 EQUALS `the most that can be awarded is` 40800
#ASSERT `What is the most I can get for loss of earning capacity` `1 Mar 2026` 52000 1000 300000 7 TRUE 141 75 EQUALS `the most that can be awarded is` 280800
-- Reg 7: ISV 7.5 is expressed as 8, over 7: 280 800; ISV 7.4 is expressed as 7: 40 800.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can get for loss of earning capacity` `1 Mar 2026` 52000 1000 300000 7.5 FALSE 141 75 EQUALS `the most that can be awarded is` 280800
#ASSERT `What is the most I can get for loss of earning capacity` `1 Mar 2026` 52000 1000 300000 7.4 FALSE 141 75 EQUALS `the most that can be awarded is` 40800
-- Past 1 000 000 and future 4 000 000: 5 000 000, capped at 4 136 000, then less 20%: 3 308 800.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can get for loss of earning capacity` `1 Mar 2026` 1000000 0 4000000 50 FALSE 141 75 EQUALS `the most that can be awarded is` 3308800
-- An accident on 1 December 2012 (finding 21, a correction): s 56A was inserted from 1 July 2013 and does not affect an
-- earlier cause of action (LSS Act Sch 2 cl 21(2)), so the 20% s 56A(5) discount and the s 56A(2) threshold must not be
-- applied: not covered. 1 July 2013, the first day: 280 800 as above.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can get for loss of earning capacity` `1 Dec 2012` 52000 1000 300000 12 FALSE 141 75 EQUALS `not covered: an accident before 1 July 2013`
#ASSERT `What is the most I can get for loss of earning capacity` `1 Jul 2013` 52000 1000 300000 12 FALSE 141 75 EQUALS `the most that can be awarded is` 280800
-- Superannuation at 12%: 280 800 x 0.12 = 33 696. Before 1 July 2013 (s 56A(6)-(9) inserted then): not covered.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can get for lost superannuation` `1 Mar 2026` 280800 0.12 EQUALS `the most that can be awarded is` 33696
#ASSERT `What is the most I can get for lost superannuation` `1 Dec 2012` 280800 0.12 EQUALS `not covered: an accident before 1 July 2013`

-- Gratuitous services (s 58, regs 18-19); reg 19 rate at 1.30: $25 x 1.3 = $32.50. Arguments: day; who; ISV; hours a
-- week; months in a row; weeks; hourly rate claimed; SAWE (HYPOTHETICAL $2 000); s 58(3); CPI March; CPI March 2013.
-- Dana's husband, 10 hours a week for 8 months, 30 weeks claimed at $40 an hour: 10 x 32.50 = 325 a week, 9 750 in all;
-- the limit is 4 x 2 000 = 8 000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can get for my family's care` `1 Mar 2026` `the spouse of the injured person` 15 10 8 30 40 2000 FALSE 130 100 EQUALS `the most that can be awarded is` 8000
-- If the court is satisfied under s 58(3): no 4-week limit; 325 a week is under SAWE: 9 750.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can get for my family's care` `1 Mar 2026` `the spouse of the injured person` 15 10 8 30 40 2000 TRUE 130 100 EQUALS `the most that can be awarded is` 9750
-- At $20 an hour (under $32.50): 10 x 20 x 30 = 6 000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can get for my family's care` `1 Mar 2026` `the spouse of the injured person` 15 10 8 30 20 2000 FALSE 130 100 EQUALS `the most that can be awarded is` 6000
-- None: a friend; ISV 10; 5 hours a week; 5 months.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can get for my family's care` `1 Mar 2026` `someone else` 15 10 8 30 40 2000 FALSE 130 100 EQUALS `the most that can be awarded is` 0
#ASSERT `What is the most I can get for my family's care` `1 Mar 2026` `the spouse of the injured person` 10 10 8 30 40 2000 FALSE 130 100 EQUALS `the most that can be awarded is` 0
#ASSERT `What is the most I can get for my family's care` `1 Mar 2026` `the spouse of the injured person` 15 5 8 30 40 2000 FALSE 130 100 EQUALS `the most that can be awarded is` 0
#ASSERT `What is the most I can get for my family's care` `1 Mar 2026` `the spouse of the injured person` 15 10 5 30 40 2000 FALSE 130 100 EQUALS `the most that can be awarded is` 0
-- Reg 7: ISV 10.5 is expressed as 11, over 10: 8 000 as above; ISV 10.4 is expressed as 10: nothing.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can get for my family's care` `1 Mar 2026` `the spouse of the injured person` 10.5 10 8 30 40 2000 FALSE 130 100 EQUALS `the most that can be awarded is` 8000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can get for my family's care` `1 Mar 2026` `the spouse of the injured person` 10.4 10 8 30 40 2000 FALSE 130 100 EQUALS `the most that can be awarded is` 0
-- An accident on 1 December 2013: $25 an hour: 10 x 25 x 30 = 7 500, under 8 000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can get for my family's care` `1 Dec 2013` `a parent of the injured person` 15 10 8 30 40 2000 FALSE 130 100 EQUALS `the most that can be awarded is` 7500
-- An accident on 1 December 2012, a spouse caring 4 hours a week for 3 months (finding 21, a correction): s 58(4) was
-- inserted from 1 July 2013 and does not affect an earlier cause of action (LSS Act Sch 2 cl 21(2)), so its 6-hour and
-- 6-month thresholds do not answer it: not covered, not 0.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can get for my family's care` `1 Dec 2012` `the spouse of the injured person` 15 4 3 13 25 2000 FALSE 130 100 EQUALS `not covered: an accident before 1 July 2013`

-- A death (ss 54(3), 58B). Arguments: day of the accident; loss assessed; earning capacity damages received; CPI Sept;
-- CPI Sept 2001.
-- 500 000 x 0.8 = 400 000.
#ASSERT `What is the most the dependants can get` `1 Mar 2026` 500000 0 141 75 EQUALS `the most that can be awarded is` 400000
-- 5 000 000 against a limit of 4 136 000 less 1 000 000 received = 3 136 000; x 0.8 = 2 508 800.
#ASSERT `What is the most the dependants can get` `1 Mar 2026` 5000000 1000000 141 75 EQUALS `the most that can be awarded is` 2508800
-- Before 1 July 2013 (s 58B inserted then; cl 21(2)): not covered.
#ASSERT `What is the most the dependants can get` `1 Dec 2012` 500000 0 141 75 EQUALS `not covered: an accident before 1 July 2013`
